# pokemon-bot

Interactive REPL chatbot over the [PokéAPI](https://pokeapi.co/), ported from the
TypeScript `/api/chat-stream` route in `open-react-template`.

## Quick start

```bash
# 1. Create a venv and install
python3 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install -e ".[test]"

# 2. Configure API keys
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env and fill in OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, KIMI_API_KEY

# 3. Run
.venv/bin/python -m pokemon_bot
```

You'll see the banner and a `you ❯` prompt. Type a question and press Enter:

```text
pokemon-bot — interactive PokéAPI assistant
Type a question and press Enter. Use /exit or Ctrl+D to quit.

you ❯ What's the speed stat of Raichu?
[status] Analysing your request…
[status] Refining query…
[status] Searching relevant data sources…
[status] Building execution plan…
[status] Running read-only queries…
[status] Generating answer…
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Raichu's speed stat is 110…
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
you ❯ /exit
```

## CLI commands

| Command | Effect |
|---|---|
| `/exit`, `/quit`, `/bye` | Leave the REPL |
| `/clear` | Reset conversation history + session |
| Ctrl+D | EOF — same as `/exit` |
| Ctrl+C | Interrupt — exit with code 130 |

The REPL keeps a multi-turn history in memory. Follow-ups like "show me its moves"
work because conversation context is fed back into the query-refinement stage.

## Environment variables

Loaded from `.env` (via `python-dotenv`) or the shell. See `.env.example` for the
template.

| Variable | Required | Default | Used by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | **Yes** | — | Every chat-completion call (planner, validator, executor synthesis, query refinement, placeholder resolver) **and** the final-answer token streaming |
| `KIMI_API_KEY` | Recommended | — | Kimi extraction step (`kimi-k2-turbo-preview`) inside the executor |
| `KIMI_BASE_URL` | No | `https://api.moonshot.cn/v1` | Kimi endpoint override |
| `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` | No | `claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929` | Anthropic model id |
| `KIMI_MODEL` | No | `moonshot-v1-32k` | Kimi model id (overridden by hard-coded `kimi-k2-turbo-preview` inside the call for parity with TS) |
| `OPENAPI_SCHEMAS_DIR` | No | (auto) | Override the OpenAPI schema directory (planner parameter mapping) |
| `PROMPTS_DIR` | No | (bundled) | Override the prompt-file directory used by `fetch_prompt_file` |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_POKEAPI_BASE_URL` | No | `https://pokeapi.co/api/v2` | PokéAPI base URL (matches the TS env name for parity) |
| `ELASTICDASH_SERVER_URL` | No | — | ElasticDash backend URL. Setting this turns on observability — the REPL calls `init_observability` at boot and wraps each chat turn in a trace. |
| `ELASTICDASH_API_KEY` | No | — | Project API key for the ElasticDash backend |
| `ELASTICDASH_DEBUG` | No | `0` | Verbose SDK logging |

## ElasticDash integration

The project uses the **`elasticdash-sdk`** Python package (import path
`elasticdash_test`) for both runtime tracing and the test framework.

1. **Tools** — every tool in `pokemon_bot/tools/pokemon_tools.py` is
   registered through `elasticdash_test.ed_tool(name=...)`. The seven
   exports (`apiService`, `queryRefinement`, `searchPokemon`,
   `fetchPokemonDetails`, `searchMove`, `searchBerry`, `searchAbility`)
   are added to the global rerun registry, so the MCP server and
   `elasticdash run-tool <name> --input '<json>'` can re-execute them
   against captured inputs. Each invocation inside an active trace is
   emitted as a `tool` WorkflowEvent.

2. **LLM calls** — captured by the SDK's httpx interceptor (installed
   automatically by `init_observability`). The `anthropic` and `openai`
   Python clients both ride on httpx, so every call from
   `kimi_chat_completion` (OpenAI client → `api.moonshot.cn/v1/chat/completions`),
   `anthropic_chat_completion`, `openai_chat_completion` (Claude dispatcher),
   and the streaming `anthropic_stream_text` is recorded as an `ai`
   WorkflowEvent without explicit decoration.

3. **Workflows** — `pokemon_bot/__main__.py` calls
   `init_observability(ObservabilityOptions(server_url=..., api_key=...))`
   once at REPL boot and `start_trace("pokemon_chat") / end_trace()`
   around each turn, so every tool + LLM event for a turn shares the
   same `trace_id`. With `ELASTICDASH_SERVER_URL` unset, both calls
   become no-ops and the REPL runs with tracing disabled.

4. **MCP server** — configured in `.mcp.json` at the project root,
   pointing at the local Node MCP at
   `/Users/jiangjiahao/Documents/GitHub/ElasticDash-MCP/mcp-server/server.ts`.
   When you open Claude Code in this directory, the
   `mcp__elasticdash-mcp__*` tools (`search_traces`, `get_trace_details`,
   `rerun_step`, `get_recent_traces`) become available automatically.

> **Migration note (2026-05-26):** the chat-completion path was switched
> from OpenAI to Anthropic Claude. `OPENAI_API_KEY` and `AI_PROVIDER` are
> no longer used — set only `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (plus `KIMI_API_KEY` for
> the extraction step). The historical `openai_chat_completion(...)`
> function name is preserved as a dispatcher that always forwards to
> Claude, so internal call sites and the planner / validator / executor
> prompts are unchanged.

## How it works

The pipeline mirrors the TypeScript `/api/chat-stream` POST handler stage-for-stage:

```text
user input
   │
   ▼
[message_utils] summarize_messages → filter_plan_messages
   │
   ▼
[handler] follow-up detection + conversation-context build
   │
   ▼
[tools/pokemon_tools] queryRefinement  ─→  Claude (system prompt: byte-identical to TS)
   │
   ▼
[chat_planner_service] get_all_matched_apis  →  get_top_k_results
   │  (static PokéAPI tool catalog, no embeddings)
   ▼
[chat/planner] send_to_planner
   │  Step 0: goal-completion check         (Claude — Claude-tuned prompt)
   │  Step 1: next-action intent             (Kimi)
   │  Step 2: keyword-based RAG retrieval
   │  Step 3: planner LLM with prompt-planner.txt  (Claude)
   ▼
[chat/validators] detect_resolution_vs_execution (Kimi)
   │
   ▼
[chat/executor] execute_iterative_planner
   │  • fetchPokemonDetails / searchPokemon / searchMove / searchAbility / searchBerry
   │  • per-step Kimi useful-data extraction
   │  • validator re-plan loop (Claude)
   │  • fan-out + depends_on_step propagation + placeholder resolution
   ▼
[handler] _stream_final_answer
   │  Claude (anthropic.messages.stream)
   ▼
stdout (one token at a time)
```

All prompts, default temperatures, max-token caps, retry counts, and stop conditions
are preserved verbatim from the TypeScript source.

## Project layout

```text
pokemon_bot/
├── __main__.py            # REPL entry point
├── config.py              # env loading
├── chat/
│   ├── handler.py         # pipeline orchestration (ports chat-stream/route.ts)
│   ├── executor.py        # iterative planner loop (ports chat/executor.ts)
│   ├── planner.py         # autonomous planner workflow
│   ├── planner_utils.py   # plan sanitiser + placeholder resolution
│   ├── validators.py      # intent classifier + goal-completion validator
│   ├── message_utils.py   # summarisation + plan-message filtering
│   └── session.py         # in-memory pending-plan store + session-id hash
├── services/
│   ├── pokemon_service.py        # PokéAPI clients (5 tools + watchlist stubs)
│   ├── api_service.py            # dynamic API request executor
│   ├── api_schema_loader.py      # OpenAPI parameter lookup
│   ├── parameter_mapper.py       # planner-param → API-param matcher (incl. fan-out)
│   ├── chat_planner_service.py   # RAG retrieval + planner support utilities
│   ├── pokemon_rag_service.py    # static PokéAPI tool catalog
│   ├── task_service.py           # task / message dataclasses
│   └── type_style_service.py     # type → Tailwind class map (frontend parity)
├── tools/
│   └── pokemon_tools.py   # named-tool registry (port of ed_tools.ts)
├── utils/
│   ├── ai_handler.py      # OpenAI / Kimi / Anthropic clients + agent runtime
│   ├── query_refinement.py
│   └── cli_stream.py      # stdout status / token writers
├── schemas/
│   └── ai.py              # pydantic models (ported from Zod schemas/ai.ts)
└── prompts/               # bundled prompt assets (planner / executor / verifier)
    ├── api-index.json
    ├── prompt-executor.txt
    ├── prompt-planner-table.txt
    ├── prompt-planner.txt
    ├── prompt-verifier.txt
    └── prompt.txt
```

